        "text": "That's sooo great Madison that  Berkeley Media Studies daily ITN put your piece first, at top, in story spotlight!\n\nThey not only listed your piece but applauded your approach: _*Much news coverage of homelessness portrays unhoused people almost exclusively as victims. This is known as deficit framing. Reporting from San Francisco Public Press uses asset-based framing to show the resilience of a man who not only was homeless but also survived a civil war and genocide in Rwanda.*_\n\nBack in February they shared with me what their reach was as I've pasted below for you. AND they have an audience that passes articles around to all their colleague on of their cross-cutting issues. Hooray ! and congrats to Madi and her editors on this.\n\n\"BMSG daily new digest (\"In the News\")\n1,792 subscribers\nOpen rate: 37%\n\nBMSG reach on social platforms:\n• Twitter \/ X followers: 3,524\n• Facebook followers: 1.4k\n• LinkedIn followers: 296 (we're just starting to get more active on this one)\"\n",
